# Test: ze config validate REFUSES a remote-id-type outside the enumeration.
# RFC 7296 Section 4 requires it be possible to configure ze to accept a PKIX
# certificate "where the ID passed is any of ID_KEY_ID, ID_FQDN, ID_RFC822_ADDR,
# or ID_DER_ASN1_DN" (RFC7296-4-4). remote-id-type is the leaf that reaches the
# two of those ze cannot derive, so the set of names it accepts is a closed
# enumeration and the YANG schema is what closes it.
#
# Deliberately NOT asserted here: that remote-id-type key-id actually permits an
# ID_KEY_ID peer to authenticate. That runs in certificateCarriesIdentity, which
# `ze config validate` never reaches -- the same boundary the dh-group parse test
# records. Unit proof: TestCfmConformanceConfigurationSetIsAcceptable and
# TestCfmConformanceSetDoesNotAcceptWhatItMustNot
# (internal/component/ike/engine/rfc7296_conformance_test.go).
# RFC requirement: RFC7296-4-4 negative -- remote-id-type is a closed set at the
# operator entry point, so a name outside the identity types RFC 7296 Section 4
# requires is refused at commit rather than silently ignored at run time.
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65533
				remote 65533
			}
		}
	}
}

vpn {
	ipsec {
		ike-group IKE-RIT {
			proposal 1 {
				encryption aes256gcm
				hash sha256
				dh-group 14
			}
		}
		esp-group ESP-RIT {
			proposal 1 {
				encryption aes256gcm
			}
		}
		site-to-site {
			peer branch-1 {
				ike-group IKE-RIT
				esp-group ESP-RIT
				local-address 127.0.0.1
				remote-address 127.0.0.2
				authentication {
					mode pre-shared-secret
					pre-shared-secret test-key-1234
					remote-id-type der-asn1-gn
				}
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=configuration invalid
expect=stdout:contains=remote-id-type
